Z||000009||rockcrawl||08-16-2000||09:14 PM||||Personally I think the whole carbon fiber thing has gotten way out of hand. It seems most poeple will add 10 pounds of carbon fiber to their car just to make it "look" faster. I doesn't make much sense to me, but the stuff does look pretty cool. I'm with filthyscarecrow on this one, for a lot less than $100 you can laminate all the parts with real carbon fiber. It's a little messy, and a little more work, but it's real. <P>I just read my own message, and it sounds like it may be a little offensive to some. Please don't get me wrong, I like rice just as much as anyone.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||1
